.Dd November 24, 2026
.Dt TRACEROUTE 1
.Os Belka
.Sh NAME
.Nm traceroute
.Nd show the routers on the way to a host
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl dIn
.Op Fl f Ar first_ttl
.Op Fl m Ar max_ttl
.Op Fl p Ar port
.Op Fl q Ar nqueries
.Op Fl s Ar src_addr
.Op Fl t Ar tos
.Op Fl w Ar waittime
.Ar host
.Op Ar packetlen
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
sends probes to
.Ar host
whose time to live rises by one at each hop, from
.Ar first_ttl ,
and prints who answers that the time ran out: the routers in turn, and
at the end the host itself.
Each hop is a line: its number, the address that answered (with its
name, unless
.Fl n
is given), and the round-trip time of each probe;
.Ql *
marks a probe nothing answered within
.Ar waittime
seconds.
A probe is a UDP datagram to a port no one is likely to use, from
.Ar port
(33434) upward, which the host answers with port unreachable; with
.Fl I ,
an ICMP echo request, which it answers with an echo reply.
An unreachable other than the host's port unreachable is marked after
the time:
.Ql !N
(network),
.Ql !H
(host),
.Ql !P
(protocol),
.Ql !F
(fragmentation needed),
.Ql !S
(source route failed),
.Ql !X
(administratively prohibited) or
.Ql !U
(other).
.Pp
The options:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl d
Accepted, and ignored.
.It Fl f Ar first_ttl
The first time to live (1).
.It Fl I
Send ICMP echo requests, not UDP datagrams.
.It Fl m Ar max_ttl
The last time to live (30).
.It Fl n
Print addresses, without looking up their names.
.It Fl p Ar port
The first UDP probe's port (33434).
.It Fl q Ar nqueries
Probes at each hop (3).
.It Fl s Ar src_addr
The probes' source address (else IP's choice).
.It Fl t Ar tos
The probes' type of service (0).
.It Fl w Ar waittime
Seconds to wait for each probe's answer (5).
.El
.Pp
.Ar packetlen
is the length of each probe in bytes, its IP header included (60).
.Pp
.Nm
needs raw sockets, which are the superuser's: it is set-user-ID root,
and gives that up once it has opened them.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when the hops were tried; 1 on an error, 2 for bad arguments.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ping 8
.Sh HISTORY
Belka's own, after Van Jacobson's traceroute of 1988.
